#
# Serves debian/bookworm instead of ubuntu/<codename> because packagecloud's
# own OS detection falls back to it on Ubuntu releases it hasn't published
# native packages for yet (confirmed: ubuntu/resolute 404s as of 2026-07-23,
# while ubuntu/noble, jammy, focal all work). EMQX bundles its own Erlang
# runtime, so the debian package installs and runs fine on Ubuntu. Do not
# "fix" this to an ubuntu/* line without first confirming that codename's
# repo actually exists — check https://packagecloud.io/emqx/emqx/ubuntu/dists/<codename>/InRelease

